  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.repositories.ShipmentRepository\": {\n        \"summary\": \"Interface for repositories holding shipment data. It defines the contract for data access operations related to shipments in the ordering system. Key methods include: `getShipments(OrderStatus status)` - retrieves a list of ShipmentRecord objects filtered by the given OrderStatus; `getShipmentById(String id)` - fetches a single ShipmentRecord by its unique identifier; `createShipment(ShipmentRecord info)` - creates a new shipment record, throwing a BadRequestException if the input is invalid; `addEvent(String id, ShipmentEventInfo event)` - appends a ShipmentEventInfo event to an existing shipment identified by id, returning a boolean indicating success; `updateShipment(ShipmentRecord info)` - updates an existing shipment record, returning a boolean indicating success; `removeShipment(String id, String eTag)` - deletes a shipment by id with optimistic concurrency control via an eTag, returning a boolean indicating success. This interface follows the Repository pattern, abstracting the underlying data store and enabling different implementations (e.g., in-memory, MongoDB).\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/repositories/ShipmentRepository.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
